1
00:00:04,615 --> 00:00:07,535
Leonard. Leonard.

2
00:00:07,701 --> 00:00:08,741
(Scene:)Leonard.

3
00:00:09,578 --> 00:00:11,618
Sheldon, it's 2:00 in the morning.

4
00:00:11,789 --> 00:00:15,169
Why does everybody keep telling me
what time it is?

5
00:00:15,334 --> 00:00:18,214
- Everybody?
- You, the president of the university...

6
00:00:18,379 --> 00:00:20,549
(Sheldon:)...his wife,
their sullen teenage daughter.

7
00:00:20,714 --> 00:00:26,594
(Sheldon:)That entire family is fascinated by what
time it is and whether people know it.

8
00:00:26,804 --> 00:00:29,844
(Leonard:)You went to President Seibert's house
in the middle of the night?

9
00:00:30,015 --> 00:00:32,935
(Sheldon:)He didn't respond to my e-mail,
his phone number is unlisted.

10
00:00:33,102 --> 00:00:35,522
(Sheldon:)Tell me what my other option was.

11
00:00:35,688 --> 00:00:37,978
(Leonard:)You could have waited until morning.

12
00:00:38,149 --> 00:00:40,899
(Leonard:)I know, look who I'm talking to.

13
00:00:42,111 --> 00:00:45,821
(Sheldon:)Remember the grant proposal I submitted
to the National Science Foundation...

14
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:48,990
(Sheldon:)...to detect slow-moving monopoles
at the magnetic north pole?

15
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:52,750
(Leonard:)Hardly a day goes by
when I don't think about it.

16
00:00:52,955 --> 00:00:54,415
Oh, how nice.

17
00:00:54,582 --> 00:00:56,962
(Sheldon:)Well, a space opened up
at the last minute...

18
00:00:57,126 --> 00:01:00,506
(Sheldon:)...on the NSF expedition
to the Arctic Circle.

19
00:01:00,671 --> 00:01:02,251
(Leonard:)Wait a minute.

